From: priangle <203159732+priangle@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:49:20 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] crt-emu: magnifier in the panel

A round lens under the F12 panel shows the screen's own pixels enlarged,
zoom x zoom each (x2 to x8, size from a slider), so the phosphor mask and
the scanlines can be seen and shot at their real size. It is dragged with
the mouse, one wheel notch over it is one zoom step, and it is shown only
while the panel is open. Near a screen edge the lens stops and the
enlarged area slides on under it to the edge; the window's undrawn extra
row (nonexclusive) is never copied. Every frame the square is copied from
the back buffer, which at that point holds only the shaded frame, and
ImGui draws it with nearest sampling (the backend's standard sampler
callbacks). Not saved.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015yjP4pBYqkzwik2NkFF1dK
